# db/migrations/**/*.sql are hash-guarded "frozen" DDL contracts: several Alembic
# migrations (e.g. apps/api/alembic/versions/20260801_0001_0002_ontology.py,
# 20260801_0004_0005_exhibition.py) compute sha256(file bytes) at upgrade time and
# refuse to run if it doesn't match a hardcoded digest, to catch accidental edits to
# a published contract. That guard breaks on any Windows checkout with the common
# core.autocrlf=true default, because autocrlf silently rewrites LF -> CRLF on
# checkout, changing every byte and therefore the hash, with no content actually
# changed. Pin these files to LF unconditionally so the digest is stable on every
# platform regardless of the checking-out machine's autocrlf setting.
db/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf
